The first eight episodes averaged more than 5.1 million multiplatform viewers.<ref>{{cite web |title=''Outlander'' Trailer: Sneak Peek At Second Half Of Starz Drama's First Season – TCA |url=https://deadline.com/2015/01/outlander-trailer-second-half-of-season-1-starz-1201345992/ |first=Anthony |last=D'Alessandro |website=Deadline Hollywood |date=January 9, 2015 |access-date=August 17, 2015 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150804091627/http://deadline.com/2015/01/outlander-trailer-second-half-of-season-1-starz-1201345992/ |archive-date=August 4, 2015 |url-status=live }}</ref> In July 2015, noting ''Outlander''{{'s}} strong ratings, its "vocal online fandom and a slew of think pieces tied to its feminist twists on the action genre", Josef Adalian of ''[[Vulture (website)|Vulture]]'' credited ''Outlander'' as one of the series responsible for [[Starz]]'s increased success against competitors like [[Showtime (TV network)|Showtime]].<ref name="Vulture 2015-07"/> On February 11, 2020, cable provider [[Comcast]] moved Starz from its base cable packages to an [[a la carte pay television|a la carte]] option. This occurred five days before the premiere of season five.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.cordcuttersnews.com/comcast-is-removing-starz-from-all-packages/|title=Comcast is Removing Starz From All TV Packages|first=Luke|last=Bouma|website=Cord Cutter News|date=January 31, 2020|access-date=May 17, 2020|archive-date=April 8, 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200408031447/https://www.cordcuttersnews.com/comcast-is-removing-starz-from-all-packages/|url-status=live}}</ref>

