'''''Portrait of a Lady on Fire''''' ({{langx|fr|Portrait de la jeune fille en feu|lit=Portrait of the Young Lady on Fire}}) is a 2019 French [[historical drama|historical]] [[romance film|romantic]] [[Drama (film and television)|drama]] film written and directed by [[Céline Sciamma]], starring [[Noémie Merlant]] and [[Adèle Haenel]]. Set in France in the late 18th century, the film tells the story of a brief affair between two young women: an aristocrat and a painter commissioned to paint her portrait. It was Haenel's final film role before retiring from the film industry in 2023.

''Portrait of a Lady on Fire'' was selected to compete for the [[Palme d'Or]] at the [[2019 Cannes Film Festival]].<ref name=CannesPalme>{{cite web|title=The 2019 Official Selection|url=https://www.festival-cannes.com/en/infos-communiques/communique/articles/the-2019-official-selection|website=[[Cannes Film Festival|Festival de Cannes]]|date=18 April 2019|access-date=9 May 2019|archive-date=16 December 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191216055752/https://www.festival-cannes.com/en/infos-communiques/communique/articles/the-2019-official-selection|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name=GuardianCannes>{{cite web|url=https://www.theguardian.com/film/2019/apr/18/cannes-festival-2019-full-list-of-films|title=Cannes festival 2019: full list of films|work=[[The Guardian]]|date=6 May 2019|access-date=18 April 2019|archive-date=8 November 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201108002255/https://www.theguardian.com/film/2019/apr/18/cannes-festival-2019-full-list-of-films|url-status=live}}</ref> The film won the [[Queer Palm]] at Cannes, becoming the first film directed by a woman to win the award.<ref name=Richford>{{cite news |last1=Richford |first1=Rhonda |title=Cannes: 'Portrait of a Lady on Fire' Takes Queer Palm Prize |work=[[The Hollywood Reporter]] |date=24 May 2019 |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/news/cannes-portrait-de-la-jeune-fille-en-feu-takes-queer-palm-prize-1213514 |access-date=25 May 2019 |archive-date=22 June 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190622204734/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/news/cannes-portrait-de-la-jeune-fille-en-feu-takes-queer-palm-prize-1213514 |url-status=live }}</ref> Sciamma also won the award for [[Cannes Film Festival Award for Best Screenplay|Best Screenplay]] at Cannes.<ref name=Cannes>{{cite web |title=Portrait de la jeune fille en feu (Portrait of a Lady on Fire) |url=https://www.festival-cannes.com/en/festival/films/portrait-de-la-jeune-fille-en-feu |website=[[Cannes Film Festival|Festival de Cannes]] |date=2019 |access-date=27 May 2019 |archive-date=16 December 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191216060409/https://www.festival-cannes.com/en/festival/films/portrait-de-la-jeune-fille-en-feu |url-status=live }}</ref><ref name=DebrugeCannes>{{cite magazine|last1=Debruge|first1=Peter|url=https://variety.com/2019/film/news/cannes-film-festival-2019-winners-1203225973/|title=Bong Joon-ho's 'Parasite' Wins the Palme d'Or at Cannes|magazine=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]|date=25 May 2019|access-date=26 May 2019|archive-date=5 June 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190605043110/https://variety.com/2019/film/news/cannes-film-festival-2019-winners-1203225973/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name=Pulver>{{cite web|last1=Pulver|first1=Andrew|url=https://www.theguardian.com/film/2019/may/25/bong-joon-hos-parasite-wins-palme-dor-at-cannes-film-festival|title=Bong Joon-ho's Parasite wins Palme d'Or at Cannes film festival|work=[[The Guardian]]|date=25 May 2019|access-date=26 May 2019|archive-date=5 June 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190605080921/https://www.theguardian.com/film/2019/may/25/bong-joon-hos-parasite-wins-palme-dor-at-cannes-film-festival|url-status=live}}</ref> The film was theatrically released in France on 18 September 2019.<ref name=JPBO />

It was nominated for [[Independent Spirit Awards]], [[25th Critics' Choice Awards|Critics' Choice Awards]] and [[77th Golden Globe Awards|Golden Globe Awards]] for Best Foreign Language Film and was chosen by the [[National Board of Review Awards 2019|National Board of Review]] as one of the top five foreign language films of 2019. The film was one of three shortlisted by the [[Ministry of Culture (France)|French Ministry of Culture]] to be France's [[List of submissions to the 92nd Academy Awards for Best International Feature Film|submission to the 92nd Academy Awards for Best International Feature Film]].<ref>{{cite web |last1=Erbland |first1=Kate |title=France's Submission for the Best International Feature Film Oscar Could Be a Game-Changer |url=https://www.indiewire.com/2019/09/oscar-submission-france-international-film-2020-1202174271/ |website=[[Indiewire]] |access-date=8 January 2020 |date=18 September 2019 |archive-date=28 December 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191228051414/https://www.indiewire.com/2019/09/oscar-submission-france-international-film-2020-1202174271/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=Sharf |first1=Zack |title='Portrait of a Lady on Fire' Loses Out on France's Oscar Pick to Ladj Ly's 'Les Miserables' |url=https://www.indiewire.com/2019/09/portrait-of-a-lady-on-fire-loses-france-oscar-pick-les-miserables-1202175146/ |publisher=[[Indiewire]] |access-date=8 January 2020 |date=20 September 2019 |archive-date=28 December 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191228051421/https://www.indiewire.com/2019/09/portrait-of-a-lady-on-fire-loses-france-oscar-pick-les-miserables-1202175146/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

